  "facts": [
   "It is the only land feature on Earth that gave its name to a constellation: Mensa ('the table'), named by Nicolas de Lacaille in the 18th century.",
   "The famous 'tablecloth' cloud forms when southeasterly wind pushes moist air up the slopes into colder air; legend blames a smoking contest between the Devil and a pirate named Van Hunks.",
   "The modern cableway cars rotate a full 360 degrees on the way up and carry 65 passengers.",
   "The mountain is flat-topped because it is a syncline: its summit rock was once the floor of a valley.",
   "About 1,500 plant species grow on Table Mountain and the Back Table alone, most of them fynbos, and the Table Mountain ghost frog lives nowhere else."
  ],
  "bestTime": "October to April (the southern summer) brings the driest, clearest days; go early, since the cableway closes when wind or the tablecloth cloud rolls in.",
  "gettingThere": "United flies nonstop from Newark to Cape Town (roughly 15 hours, a few times a week); from the city the cableway's lower station is about a 15-minute drive.",
  "tip": "Check the cableway's live status before heading up, as it shuts in high wind; fit hikers can climb Platteklip Gorge, the route of the first recorded ascent in 1503, in about 2.5 hours."
